# Caddy in front of Kennwort (K-703, docs/installation.md): gets the TLS certificate and passes
# everything to the server unchanged. The server serves the web app itself and sets every security
# header (docs/sicherheitsdesign.md, P-16, "CSP und Sicherheits-Kopfzeilen"), HSTS included with
# KENNWORT_PUBLIC_URL on https. This file sets none: two CSP headers would both apply, and two
# Strict-Transport-Security headers are an error. To serve the web build from Caddy instead, take
# Caddyfile.static, which sends exactly the headers of the table.
{$KENNWORT_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy kennwort:8100
}
